    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe default tabline still uses a dedicated C renderer, while custom tablines\nalready use the statusline expression engine. Users who only want to customize\nindividual tab labels must therefore replace the complete tabline and recreate\nits highlights, click targets, showcmd area, and close button.\n\n## Solution\n\nGenerate the default tabline as an expression in Lua and render it with the\nexisting statusline/tabline engine, following the migration used by the default\nstatusline. Keep tab highlights, click handling, whole-line truncation, showcmd,\nand the close button in the existing expression renderer.\n\nAllow `vim._core.tabline.default()` to take an optional Lua item formatter. The\nformatter receives the current tab number, tabpage, and selected window, so a\nconfiguration can change labels without rebuilding the rest of the tabline.\n\nReferences #19272.\n\nTests:\n\n- `zig build functionaltest -- test/functional/ui/tabline_spec.lua`\n- `zig build functionaltest -- test/functional/ui/statusline_spec.lua`\n- `zig build functionaltest -- --filter 'can override Tabline' test/functional/ui/highlight_spec.lua`\n- `zig build functionaltest -- --filter tabline test/functional/ui/mouse_spec.lua`\n- `zig build oldtest -- test_tabline.vim`\n- `zig build lintc-uncrustify`\n- `zig build`\n",
